From fb900c54dd09a8b1c4d84b9fc5afc7f67b3b6af6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raeli Savitt <raeli.savitt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 16:08:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add usemod adapter (UseModWiki/ProWiki/Oddmuse action=rc) +
 cadence on item timestamps

- idx_usemod parses the RecentChanges HTML list these CGI engines emit
  (English/German date headers, 24h/am-pm times, [summary], author/IP);
  id = hash(page, date, time, author) since there is no revid.
- cadence now uses the item's own ts when the venue provides one, so a
  first tick over a 30-day listing does not count all history as one hour.
- test_usemod.py: mock UseMod + ProWiki listings.
- README/venues.json: document usemod and jsonlist adapters.
